<title>FRANCE: EP calls for directive on worker participation.</title>
<headline>EP calls for directive on worker participation.</headline>
<dateline>STRASBOURG 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Parliament on Friday urged the European Commission to urgently draft proposals to improve workers' participation in decision-making.</p>
<p>Responding to a Commission communication on worker information and consultation, COM(95)547, Euro-MPs said the Commission should now go further and propose concrete measures.</p>
<p>These included a directive which sets out a general legal framework for worker participation and imposed minimum standards of consultation and information.</p>
<p>The adoption of a European statute for companies should not allow them to avoid employee representation, Euro-MPs said.</p>
</text>
